<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Kevod Rabo v'Talmid Chacham 1</div>

<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">"מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְתָּ וְכוּ' וְיָרֵאתָ מֵאֱלֹקֶיךָ וְכוּ'". אֵין שֵׂיבָה פָּחוֹת מִשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנָה: וְעַיֵּן בַּמַּאֲמָר "פָּתַח רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן" ((בְּסִימָן ס), מְבֹאָר שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת שִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת שִׁבְעִים פָּנִים, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נַעֲשֶׂה הִתְעוֹרְרוּת הַשֵּׁנָה, וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זוֹכִין לְיִרְאָה, עַיֵּן שָׁם: וְזֶהוּ רֶמֶז מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם. כִּי כְּשֶׁרוֹאֶה פְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה בֶּן שִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה, בְּחִינַת שִׁבְעִים פָּנִים, מְחֻיָּב לָקוּם וּלְהִתְעוֹרֵר בִּבְחִינַת הִתְעוֹרְרוּת הַשֵּׁנָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, מָתַי תָּקוּם מִשְּׁנָתֶךָ. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת וְהָדַרְתָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן, כִּי זֶה בְּחִינַת הַדְרַת פָּנִים, שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת כְּלָלִיּוּת כָּל הַשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנִים שִׁבְעִים פָּנִים, כַּמְבֹאָר שָׁם, עַיֵּן שָׁם. וְהַיְנוּ דְּסִיֵּם 'וְיָרֵאתָ מֵאֱלֹקֶיךָ', כִּי עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זוֹכִין לְיִרְאָה כַּנַּ"ל, עַיֵּן שָׁם:</div>

<p class="first"><span class="verse-inline">"Before an elder you shall rise, and you shall honor</span> etc. <span class="verse-inline">and you shall fear your G-d"</span> etc. <span class="verse-source">(Leviticus 19:32)</span>. <span class="verse-inline">"An elder (<em>saivah</em>) is no less than seventy years."</span></p>

<p>And see the <em>ma'amar</em> <span class="verse-inline">"<em>Pasach Rabbi Shimon</em>"</span> (Torah 60), where it is explained that through the aspect of seventy years — which are the aspect of seventy faces (<em>shiv'im panim</em>) — through this the awakening of sleep is accomplished. And through this one merits <em>yirah</em>; see there.</p>

<p>And this is the allusion of <span class="verse-inline">"Before an elder (<em>saivah</em>) you shall rise."</span> For when one sees the face of an elder who is seventy years old — the aspect of seventy faces — one is obligated to rise and to awaken, in the aspect of the awakening of sleep, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"When will you rise from your sleep?"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Proverbs 6:9)</span>.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"and you shall honor (<em>v'hadarta</em>) the face of an elder (<em>zakain</em>)."</span> For this is the aspect of <em>hadras panim</em> <span class="added">[the splendor of the face]</span>, which is the aspect of the inclusiveness of all the seventy years, the seventy faces — as is explained there; see there.</p>

<p>And this is why the verse concludes, <span class="verse-inline">"and you shall fear your G-d."</span> For through this one merits <em>yirah</em>, as mentioned above; see there.</p>

