<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Kevod Rabo v'Talmid Chacham 2</div>

<!-- ══════════ Introduction ══════════ -->
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew (intro)</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">עִנְיַן קִימָה וְהִדּוּר מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה וְזָקֵן, עִנְיַן יִרְאַת רַבּוֹ וּכְבוֹדוֹ: עַל-פִּי הַמְבֹאָר בַּמַּאֲמָר "חוֹתָם בְּתוֹךְ חוֹתָם" ((סִימָן כב) שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּחִינַת נַעֲשֶׂה וְנִשְׁמָע, שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינַת נִגְלֶה וְנִסְתָּר, בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָה וּתְפִלָּה, בְּחִינַת בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא, מַאֲמָר וַחֲצִי מַאֲמָר: וְהַכְּלָל הַיּוֹצֵא מִשָּׁם שֶׁנִּגְלֶה הוּא בְּחִינַת נַעֲשֶׂה. וְנִסְתָּר הוּא בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת תְּפִלָּה, בְּחִינַת בְּרֵאשִׁית יָרֵא בֹּשֶׁת, בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה, בְּחִינַת תּוֹרַת ה'. וְכָל אֶחָד צָרִיךְ לִרְאוֹת לַעֲשׂוֹת מֵהַנִּשְׁמָע נַעֲשֶׂה, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁיִּזְכֶּה לְהַשִּיג וּלְהָבִין אֶת בְּחִינַת הַנִּסְתָּר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת תְּפִלָּה וְכוּ', שֶׁיִּהְיֶה נַעֲשֶׂה מֵהַנִּשְׁמָע נַעֲשֶׂה מֵהַנִּסְתָּרוֹת נִגְלוֹת וְכוּ', עַיֵּן שָׁם הֵיטֵב:</div>

<p class="first">The matter of <strong>rising and <em>hidur</em> before an elder (<em>saivah</em>) and a <em>zakain</em></strong>, the matter of the fear of one's Rav and his honor. According to what is explained in the <em>ma'amar</em> <span class="verse-inline">"<em>Chosam b'soch chosam</em>"</span> <span class="added">[a seal within a seal]</span> (Torah 22): that there is the aspect of <em>na'aseh</em> and <em>nishma</em> <span class="added">[we will do and we will hear]</span>, which are the aspect of the revealed (<em>nigleh</em>) and the hidden (<em>nistar</em>), the aspect of Torah and <em>tefilah</em>, the aspect of <em>Beraishis bara</em> — a <em>ma'amar</em> <span class="added">[utterance]</span> and a half-<em>ma'amar</em>.</p>

<p>And the general principle that emerges from there is that the <em>nigleh</em> is the aspect of <em>na'aseh</em>. And the <em>nistar</em> is the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>tefilah</em>, the aspect of <em>Beraishis</em> — <em>yarai boshes</em> <span class="added">[fear of shame]</span>, the aspect of <em>amidah</em> <span class="added">[standing]</span>, the aspect of <em>Toras Hashem</em>. And each person must strive to make from the <em>nishma</em> a <em>na'aseh</em> — that is, that he should merit to grasp and understand the aspect of the <em>nistar</em>, which is the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>tefilah</em> etc. — that the <em>nishma</em> should become <em>na'aseh</em>, that the hidden things should become revealed etc.; see there well.</p>

<!-- ══════════ Section 1 ══════════ -->
<span class="section-num">1.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 1</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְהִנֵּה מַה שֶּׁמְּקַבְּלִין מֵהָרַבִּי, זֶה בְּחִינַת שֶׁמֵּאִיר עֵינָיו וּמַכְנִיס בּוֹ אֶת בְּחִינַת הַנִּשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת הַנִּסְתָּר, שֶׁיִּהְיֶה נַעֲשֶׂה אֶצְלוֹ בְּחִינַת נִגְלֶה, כִּי הָרַב מְגַלֶּה לוֹ הַנִּסְתָּר וּמְבָאֵר לוֹ כָּל הַסְּתוּמוֹת וְהַנִּסְתָּרוֹת מִמֶּנּוּ שֶׁהָיוּ מִתְּחִלָּה בִּבְחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בִּבְחִינַת נִסְתָּר אֶצְלוֹ. וְעַל-יְדֵי הָרַב נִתְגַּלֶּה לוֹ הַנִּסְתָּר מִמֶּנּוּ וְנַעֲשֶׂה אֶצְלוֹ בְּחִינַת נִגְלֶה. וְעַל-כֵּן חַיָּב הַתַּלְמִיד לִירֹא מִמֶּנּוּ, כִּי שָׁם בִּבְחִינַת הָרַב הוּא בְּחִינַת הַיִּרְאָה, שֶׁהִוא בְּחִינַת בְּרֵאשִׁית יָרֵא בֹּשֶׁת, בְּחִינַת תְּפִלָּה, בְּחִינַת נִסְתָּר. כִּי הָרַב אֵצֶל הַתַּלְמִיד הוּא בִּבְחִינַת נִסְתָּר, בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת יִרְאָה. כִּי הַשָּגַת הָרַב הִיא נִסְתָּר אֵצֶל הַתַּלְמִיד וְעַל-יְדֵי הָרַב נִתְגַּלֶּה לְהַתַּלְמִיד מַה שֶּׁהָיָה נִסְתָּר מִמֶּנּוּ כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן חַיָּב שֶׁיִּהְיֶה לְהַתַּלְמִיד יִרְאָה מֵהָרַב, כִּי שָׁם מְקוֹם הַיִּרְאָה בִּבְחִינַת הַנִּסְתָּר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת תְּפִלָּה, בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת בְּרֵאשִׁית יָרֵא בֹּשֶׁת כַּנַּ"ל: וְעַל-כֵּן חַיָּב לַעֲמֹד בִּפְנֵי הָרַב, כִּי שָׁם בִּבְחִינַת הָרַב הוּא בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה שֶׁהִוא בְּחִינַת נִסְתָּר, בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת תְּפִלָּה, בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה, כַּמְבֹאָר שָׁם הֵיטֵב. שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת בִּימֵי רַבָּן גַּמְלִיאֵל הָיוּ לוֹמְדִים תּוֹרָה בַּעֲמִידָה, עַיֵּן שָׁם הֵיטֵב:</div>

<p class="first">And behold, what one receives from the Rebbe — this is the aspect of illuminating his eyes and instilling in him the aspect of the <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of the <em>nistar</em>, so that it becomes for him the aspect of the <em>nigleh</em>. For the Rav reveals to him the hidden and explains to him all the sealed and hidden matters that were at first in the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, in the aspect of <em>nistar</em> for him. And through the Rav, the <em>nistar</em> is revealed to him and becomes for him the aspect of <em>nigleh</em>.</p>

<p>And therefore <strong>the student is obligated to fear him</strong> <span class="added">[the Rav]</span>. For there, in the aspect of the Rav, is the aspect of <em>yirah</em> — which is the aspect of <em>Beraishis</em>, <em>yarai boshes</em>, the aspect of <em>tefilah</em>, the aspect of <em>nistar</em>. For the Rav, in relation to the student, is in the aspect of <em>nistar</em>, the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>yirah</em>. For the Rav's attainment is <em>nistar</em> in relation to the student. And through the Rav, what was hidden from the student is revealed to him, as mentioned above. And therefore the student must have <em>yirah</em> of the Rav — for there is the place of <em>yirah</em>, in the aspect of the <em>nistar</em>, which is the aspect of <em>tefilah</em>, the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>Beraishis</em>, <em>yarai boshes</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore <strong>one is obligated to stand before the Rav</strong>. For there, in the aspect of the Rav, is the aspect of <em>amidah</em> <span class="added">[standing]</span>, which is the aspect of <em>nistar</em>, the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>tefilah</em>, the aspect of <em>amidah</em> — as is explained there well. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse-inline">"In the days of Rabban Gamliel, they would study Torah while standing"</span>; see there well.</p>

<!-- ══════════ Section 2 ══════════ -->
<span class="section-num">2.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 2</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת קִימָה בִּפְנֵי הֶחָכָם וְהַזָּקֵן, כִּי זָקֵן זֶה קָנָה חָכְמָה. 'קָנָה' דַּיְקָא, הַיְנוּ שֶׁקָּנָה וְהִשִּיג מַה שֶּׁהָיָה נֶעְלַם מִמֶּנּוּ, שֶׁזָּכָה לִיגַע עַד שֶׁהִשִּיג אֶת בְּחִינַת הַנִּשְׁמָע וְהַנִּסְתָּר, וְעָשָׂה מֵהַנִּשְׁמָע נַעֲשֶׂה. שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה קָנָה אֶת הַחָכְמָה לִהְיוֹת שֶׁלּוֹ, כִּי מִתְּחִלָּה הִיא תּוֹרַת ה' וְעַכְשָׁו הִיא תּוֹרָתוֹ, כְּמוֹ שֶׁדָּרְשׁוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ"ל, וְכַמְבֹאָר עִנְיָן זֶה הֵיטֵב בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ"ל. כִּי הַנִּשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת הַנִּסְתָּר, הִיא בְּחִינַת תּוֹרַת ה'. וְהַנַּעֲשֶׂה, הַיְנוּ הַנִּגְלֶה, הִיא בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָתוֹ. וּכְשֶׁזּוֹכֶה לְהַשִּיג הַנִּסְתָּר, אֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה מִתּוֹרַת ה' בְּחִינַת תּוֹרָתוֹ, וְעַל-כֵּן נִקְרָא זָקֵן זֶה קָנָה חָכְמָה, 'קָנָה' דַּיְקָא, כִּי קָנָה לִהְיוֹת שֶׁלּוֹ לִהְיוֹת נִקְרָא תּוֹרָתוֹ, עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁיָּגַע וּמָצָא וְעָשָׂה מֵהַנִּשְׁמָע נַעֲשֶׂה, מֵהַנִּסְתָּר נִגְלֶה, מִבְּחִינַת תּוֹרַת ה' תּוֹרָתוֹ כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן חַיָּבִים לָקוּם וְלַעֲמֹד מִפָּנָיו, כִּי מֵאַחַר שֶׁזָּכָה לִבְחִינַת הַנִּשְׁמָע, כִּי זָכָה לְהַשִּיג אֶת בְּחִינַת הַנִּסְתָּר שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה, עַל-כֵּן חַיָּבִים לַעֲמֹד מִפָּנָיו, כִּי שָׁם בִּבְחִינַת הַנִּשְׁמַע הוּא בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה כַּנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of <strong>rising before the <em>chacham</em> and the <em>zakain</em></strong>. For <span class="verse-inline">"<em>zakain</em> — this is one who has acquired (<em>kanah</em>) wisdom."</span> <em>"Kanah"</em> specifically — that is, that he acquired and grasped what was hidden from him. He merited exerting himself until he grasped the aspect of the <em>nishma</em> and the <em>nistar</em>, and he made from the <em>nishma</em> a <em>na'aseh</em>.</p>

<p>Through this, he acquired the wisdom to be his own — for at first it was <em>Toras Hashem</em> <span class="added">[the Torah of Hashem]</span>, and now it is <em>Toraso</em> <span class="added">[his Torah]</span>, as our Sages of blessed memory expounded, and as this matter is explained well in the aforementioned <em>ma'amar</em>. For the <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of the <em>nistar</em>, is the aspect of <em>Toras Hashem</em>. And the <em>na'aseh</em>, that is the <em>nigleh</em>, is the aspect of <em>Toraso</em>. And when he merits grasping the <em>nistar</em>, then it transforms from <em>Toras Hashem</em> to the aspect of <em>Toraso</em>.</p>

<p>And therefore he is called <em>"zakain zeh kanah chochmah"</em> — <em>"kanah"</em> specifically. For he acquired it to be his own, to be called <em>Toraso</em> — through exerting himself and finding, and making from the <em>nishma</em> a <em>na'aseh</em>, from the <em>nistar</em> a <em>nigleh</em>, from the aspect of <em>Toras Hashem</em> — <em>Toraso</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore one is obligated to rise and stand before him. For since he merited the aspect of the <em>nishma</em> — for he merited grasping the aspect of the <em>nistar</em>, which is the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>amidah</em> — therefore one is obligated to stand before him. For there, in the aspect of the <em>nishma</em>, is the aspect of <em>amidah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ══════════ Section 3 ══════════ -->
<span class="section-num">3.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 3</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶהוּ גַּם כֵּן בְּחִינַת קִימָה מִפְּנֵי הַשֵּיבָה אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁאֵינוֹ חָכָם, כִּי אֵין שֵׂיבָה פָּחוֹת מִשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנָה, כִּי כָּל הַשָּׁנִים שֶׁל חַיֵּי הָאָדָם, כֻּלָּם מְקַבְּלִים חִיּוּת מֵהַתּוֹרָה שֶׁהִיא חַיֵּינוּ וְאֹרֶךְ יָמֵינוּ, וְיֵשׁ שִׁבְעִים פָּנִים לַתּוֹרָה, וּמִשָּׁם מְקַבְּלִים חִיּוּת הַשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנִים שֶׁל הָאָדָם. אַךְ יֵשׁ סִתְרֵי פְּנִימִיּוּת הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁהֵם לְמַעְלָה מֵהַשִּׁבְעִים פָּנִים שֶׁל הַתּוֹרָה, וְהֵם בְּחִינַת הַדְרַת פָּנִים, שֶׁהֵם לְמַעְלָה מִכָּל הַשִּׁבְעִים פָּנִים, מִכָּל הַשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנִים. וְכַמּוּבָן זֶה בַּמַּאֲמָר "פָּתַח רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן וְאָמַר עֵת לַעֲשׂוֹת לַה'" וְכוּ', עַיֵּן שָׁם ((סִימָן ס). וְאֵלּוּ הַנִּסְתָּרוֹת שֶׁהֵם לְמַעְלָה מֵהַשִּׁבְעִים פָּנִים, מִשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנִים, הֵם בְּחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת נִסְתָּר כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן מִי שֶׁזָּכָה לְשֵׂיבָה וְעָבַר עַל כָּל הַשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנָה, נִמְצָא שֶׁהוּא מְקַבֵּל עַכְשָׁו חִיּוּת מִבְּחִינַת הַדְרַת פָּנִים, מִבְּחִינַת נִסְתָּר שֶׁהוּא לְמַעְלָה מִשִּׁבְעִים פָּנִים, מִשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנִים כַּנַּ"ל. עַל-כֵּן חַיָּבִין לְהַדְּרוֹ וְלָקוּם מִפָּנָיו, כִּי שָׁם לְמַעְלָה מִשִּׁבְעִים שָׁנָה לְמַעְלָה מִשִּׁבְעִים פָּנִים, הוּא בְּחִינַת הַדְרַת פָּנִים, בְּחִינַת עֲמִידָה. וְעַל-כֵּן חַיָּבִין לְהַדֵּר וְלַעֲמֹד מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה וְזָקֵן כַּנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is also the aspect of <strong>rising before the elder (<em>saivah</em>) even though he is not a <em>chacham</em></strong>. For <span class="verse-inline">"an elder (<em>saivah</em>) is no less than seventy years."</span> For all the years of a person's life — all of them receive vitality from the Torah, which is <span class="verse-inline">"our life and the length of our days"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Deuteronomy 30:20)</span>. And there are seventy faces to the Torah, and from there the seventy years of a person receive vitality.</p>

<p>But there are inner secrets of the Torah (<em>sisrai penimiyus haTorah</em>) that are above the seventy faces of the Torah. And they are the aspect of <em>hadras panim</em> <span class="added">[the splendor of the face]</span>, which are above all the seventy faces, above all the seventy years — as is understood from the <em>ma'amar</em> <span class="verse-inline">"<em>Pasach Rabbi Shimon v'amar: Ais la'asos laHashem</em>"</span> etc.; see there (Torah 60).</p>

<p>And these hidden matters that are above the seventy faces, above the seventy years — they are the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>amidah</em>, which is the aspect of <em>nistar</em>, as mentioned above. And therefore, one who merited reaching <em>saivah</em> and has passed through all the seventy years — it turns out that he now receives vitality from the aspect of <em>hadras panim</em>, from the aspect of the <em>nistar</em>, which is above the seventy faces, above the seventy years, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore one is obligated to honor him (<em>l'hadro</em>) and to rise before him. For there, above seventy years, above seventy faces, is the aspect of <em>hadras panim</em>, the aspect of <em>amidah</em>. And therefore one is obligated to give <em>hidur</em> and to stand before the elder (<em>saivah</em>) and the <em>zakain</em>, as mentioned above.</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 4 ══════════ -->
<span class="section-num">4.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 4</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">גַם הַכָּבוֹד שֶׁמְּחֻיָּבִין לְכַבֵּד אֶת הָרַב וְהַזָּקֵן, הוּא בִּכְלַל הַיִּרְאָה שֶׁהִיא שַׁיָּכָה לְהָרַב וְהַזָּקֵן שֶׁהוּא בִּבְחִינַת נִשְׁמָע וְכוּ' כַּנַּ"ל. כִּי הַכָּבוֹד נִכְלָל בִּכְלַל הַיִּרְאָה, כִּי הַיִּרְאָה הִיא שֹׁרֶשׁ הַכָּבוֹד, כַּמְבֹאָר בְּדִבְרֵי רַבֵּנוּ זֵכֶר צַדִּיק לִבְרָכָה הֲרֵינִי כַּפָּרַת מִשְׁכָּבוֹ ((סִימָן יד). וּכְמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב ((תְּהִלִּים טו), וְאֶת יִרְאֵי ה' יְכַבֵּד, וְעַל-כֵּן הַכָּבוֹד הוּא בִּכְלַל הַיִּרְאָה, שֶׁהִיא בִּבְחִינַת הָרַב וְהַזָּקֵן שֶׁהֵם בִּבְחִינַת נִשְׁמָע, בְּחִינַת יִרְאָה, בְּחִינַת יִרְאָה כַּנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">Also, the <strong><em>kavod</em> that one is obligated to give to the Rav and the <em>zakain</em></strong> is included within the <em>yirah</em> that pertains to the Rav and the <em>zakain</em>, who is in the aspect of <em>nishma</em> etc., as mentioned above. For the <em>kavod</em> is included within the <em>yirah</em> — for the <em>yirah</em> is the root of the <em>kavod</em>, as is explained in the words of our Rebbe of blessed memory, may I be an atonement for his resting place (Torah 14). And as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"and those who fear Hashem he honors"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 15:4)</span>. And therefore the <em>kavod</em> is included within the <em>yirah</em>, which is in the aspect of the Rav and the <em>zakain</em>, who are in the aspect of <em>nishma</em>, the aspect of <em>yirah</em>, the aspect of <em>yirah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

<hr>

<div class="translator-summary">
<h3>Translator's Summary</h3>
<p><strong>Kevod Rabo 1 (LM I:60):</strong> "Mipnai saivah takum" — saivah = 70 years = 70 panim (faces of the Torah). Seeing the face of the seventy-year-old triggers his'orerus hashaynah (awakening from sleep). "V'hadarta pnai zakain" = hadras panim = the inclusiveness of all 70 faces. Concludes with "v'yaraisa mai'Elokecha" — for through this one merits yirah.</p>
<p><strong>Kevod Rabo 2 (LM I:22 — "Chosam b'soch chosam"):</strong> Na'aseh/nishma = nigleh/nistar = Torah/tefilah = Beraishis = ma'amar and half-ma'amar. §1: The Rebbe reveals the nistar to the talmid, making nishma into na'aseh. Therefore yirah of the Rav (Rav = nistar = yirah = Beraishis yarai boshes) and amidah before the Rav (amidah = nistar = tefilah = nishma). §2: "Zakain zeh kanah chochmah" — kanah specifically: he exerted until the nistar became nigleh, transforming Toras Hashem into Toraso. Therefore one stands before him = amidah = nishma. §3: Even saivah who isn't a chacham — past 70 years = receiving from hadras panim (above 70 faces = above 70 years = nistar). Therefore obligated in hidur and kimah.</p>
</div>

